    board: file CF-082 — a decimal disk floor is truncated down, so admission enforces less than the operator wrote
    
    QA lane row from code-factory-releng-qa (tick 2026-11-03-15-39-07), measured at origin/main 85ed919.
    
    scripts/disk_floor.py accepts decimal sizes (docstring: "int / <int>G / <int>GiB / <decimal>G") but
    converts them with int(float(...)) at :66 and int(raw) at :55, so 5.9G resolves to floor_gib 5 with
    source=cli — the operator's number silently lowered, while the docstring promises "a typo must not
    lower a floor". scripts/lib.sh require_disk then compares df's float free space against the truncated
    integer: with 5.5 GB free and a 5.9G floor requested, it prints
      PASS  disk — 5.5 GB free (floor 5 GB)
    and admits the host. The row carries a re-runnable probe that prints exactly that.
    
